# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Repository layout
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  The repo root is the GitHub Pages deploy target: Pages is configured to
#  deploy `main/root` as a branch build, and changing that setting requires
#  repo admin access. So `index.html`, `assets/` and friends at the root ARE
#  build output and must be committed.
#
#  The Vite project lives in `app/`:
#     cd app && npm install && npm run dev
#     cd app && npm run build
#
#  The GitHub Actions workflow builds `app/` and copies the result to the root
#  on every push, so the committed output stays in step with the source.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Never committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
app/node_modules/
app/dist/

# Local secrets. `.env.example` IS committed — it holds placeholders only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Committed, but noisy
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output from `app/` lands at the root and is committed on purpose. These
# two patterns stop git from reporting the whole tree as changed when it
# rebuilds, without hiding a real source edit.